From: Fountain5405 <Fountain5405@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:15:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/27] tests: a mined block with a dishonest coinbase

gen_bad_miner_tx_in_block builds, on the same parent and with the same
1 or 17 valid transactions, a block whose coinbase over-mints by the
block reward or claims the fees plus one, and the honest block. The
generator mines both, so the bad block fails on its coinbase, not on
proof of work. The bad block must be refused and the honest one
accepted.

At hf16 the coinbase carries plain amounts with no output commitments,
so there is no commitment to tamper with; that case waits for
HF_VERSION_CARROT.

Four instances.

Written by the second reviewer; adopted here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
